{{- /*
retry-marker: the "# retry:" comment line of an install script. Input: dict with
chezmoi (.chezmoi) and name (the script's marker name, e.g. "50-claude").
It prints the nonce the script's last failed run wrote into
~/.local/state/develop-env/retry/<name>, or nothing when no retry is pending.
Every failure writes a new nonce, so the rendered script changes after each
failed run and chezmoi (which keys run_onchange_ scripts by content) runs it
again on the next apply; a clean run deletes the marker. Pair it with
retry-sh (sh) or retry-ps1 (PowerShell). Use:
  {{ template "retry-marker" (dict "chezmoi" .chezmoi "name" "50-claude") }}
*/ -}}
{{ $m := joinPath .chezmoi.homeDir ".local/state/develop-env/retry" .name }}# retry: {{ if stat $m }}{{ include $m | trim }}{{ end }}